  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes spelled \"Luka\"). Here's a summary of what's known about this place:\n\n- **Iuka** (/a\u026a\u02c8ju\u02d0k\u0259/) is a city in and the county seat of **Tishomingo County, Mississippi**, United States.\n\n- Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census.\n\n- **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n- Iuka is built on the site of a **Chickasaw village**, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of that village.\n\n- Iuka was founded by **David Hubbard**, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the Memphis and Charleston Railroad in **1857**.\n\n- The **Civil War** brought widespread devastation when a major engagement occurred on **September 19, 1862** \u2014 the Battle of Iuka \u2014 resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n- Iuka is located in **northeast Mississippi**, with U.S. Route 72 running through the southern part of the city.\n\n- There is also a **Luka Springs** \u2014 a public drinking spring \u2014 located in the area (Luka, MS 38852).\n\nIs there something specific about Iuka/Luka, Mississippi you'd like to know more about? \ud83d\ude0a",
